it true), as PyErr_Print's handle_system_exit; a file that does not open: \"Could not open"] [273 1 "// PYTHONSTARTUP\" and its OSError printed."] [316 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [317 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [320 1 "// mModeFile and stdinModeFile are the files bin/pyi python writes for -m and for a program read from stdin (queue 250)."] [326 1 "// startSafePath is -P (safe_path) as bin/pyi python's command line gave it (PYI_SAFE_PATH: 1 under -P or -I, 0"] [327 1 "// without, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is); -1 when not run by bin/pyi python (bin/pyi"] [328 1 "// run's programs and the check's driver, whose sys.flags.safe_path is the reference driver's -P)."] [349 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [350 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [355 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [356 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [357 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when the file reads) and"] [358 1 "// \"Type: text\", a SyntaxError's location and caret, the notes. Carets under expressions are not"] [359 1 "// printed (PY5b: a recorded difference)."] [360 1 "//"] [361 1 "// The text goes to sys.stderr (PyErr_Display's file): the process's standard error while sys.stderr is"] [362 1 "// the one it started with, else the text is written by sys.stderr.write and flushed (support.captured_stderr),"] [363 1 "// nothing when sys.stderr is None or missing, write's errors ignored."] [377 1 "// PrintUncaught is PyErr_Print (Python/pythonrun.c's _PyErr_PrintEx with set_sys_last_vars, queue 223): an uncaught"] [378 1 "// exception, not SystemExit, stored as sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback, then given to"] [379 1 "// sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback); \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the display when it is absent or None; when"] [380 1 "// the hook raises, \"Error in sys.excepthook:\", that error's display, then \"Original exception was:\" and the original's."] [387 22 "// after the main module's run: the hook runs on the main thread"] [402 2 "// _PyErr_PrintEx's audit (queue 536): a hook's RuntimeError ends the display, another error is unraisable"] [426 1 "// registerCode is run_mod's interactive source (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): -c's code and its nested code objects"] [427 1 "// registered by linecache._register_code(code, source, name), so traceback's display shows -c's lines; an error dropped."] [441 1 "// displayByTraceback is _PyErr_Display's first way (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): the stdlib's"] [442 1 "// traceback._print_exception_bltin(exc), Lib/traceback.py's display with its caret lines (PEP 657's positions,"] [443 1 "// co_positions), chains, groups and notes; false when the module or its function is missing or the call raised (the"] [444 1 "// error dropped, as PyErr_Clear), the caller then printing the Go display (print_exception_recursive's fallback)."] [445 1 "// Not while traceback itself is being imported or displaying (a second error then printed by the fallback)."] [477 1 "// writeStderr writes text to sys.stderr: in.Stderr when it is the original stream."] [517 4 "// at shutdown CPython's display reads no source (the import of io fails: queue 253)"] [526 1 "// FormatExceptionOnly is traceback.format_exception_only's text: a SyntaxError's location, source"] [527 1 "// line and caret, then \"Type: text\" (the type qualified by its module unless builtins), then the notes."] [532 23 "// traceback's stype: the module unless __main__ or builtins"] [536 3 "// str(exc) (traceback's _safe_string): a class's own __str__"] [616 1 "// RegisterSource gives sourceLine the text of a source that is no file (\"<s